# What must not reach an image build context.
#
# `node_modules/` is the one that matters: the app image runs
# `bun install --frozen-lockfile` for the target platform, and copying a host
# tree over it would ship this machine's binaries — PGlite's WASM among them —
# into a container that may not share the architecture.
node_modules/

# A local record. It is gitignored, it can be gigabytes, and an image that
# shipped one would hand every container a copy of somebody's project.
.labkit/

# Build output and the leak `scripts/build-binary.sh` exists to contain: a
# `bun build --compile` leaves a byte-identical copy of the bun binary behind
# on every successful run, and thirty-two of them once reached 1.9GB here.
bin/
*.bun-build

.git/
docs/
